#!/usr/bin/env bash
# PreToolUse hook — the floor of the spec-driven workflow (specs/spec-driven-workflow, ADR-003;
# approval hardened in specs/hook-owned-approval, ADR-001; the cycle's limits and the record
# rules added in specs/factory-cycle, hardened by its round-1 review).
#
# One principle runs through every rule here: deny what the model can write, record what only
# the person can do. The model writes source, specs, reviews and reports; it cannot answer a
# permission prompt, type a slash command, or be two roles at once — and those are the three
# things the records below are keyed on.
#
# Praxis primes; it did not gate. The measured evaluation recorded what priming alone buys
# for the record of a change: 0 Run Cards in 8/8 `full` cells. A prose rule saying "write the
# spec first" travels the same channel and gets the same result. So the one invariant the
# owner asked for — every change leaves `specs/<change>/`, in every mode — is held here,
# mechanically, and scaled by the dial:
#
#   fast        `specs/<active>/implementation.md` exists
#   full        `specs/<active>/spec.md` (a legacy `design.md` is accepted) and
#               `implementation.md` exist, AND the person approved the spec:
#               `.praxis/approved/<active>` exists → allow, whatever `stage:` says. No marker →
#               the ONE approval stop, as the host's own primitive, `permissionDecision: "ask"`.
#               When the person approves, the edit runs and `post-tool-use` writes the marker;
#               the floor never asks again. No spec → deny, naming the file to write.
#
# Why a marker and not `stage:`: evals/floor measured 3/3 unattended `full` runs setting
# `stage: planned` themselves after the host refused the `ask`, then building. The ledger is
# a field the model owns; the marker is written by a hook after an edit the person allowed,
# or by the person through `/praxis:approve <change>`. In `claude -p` the host refuses `ask` —
# that is the intended outcome: an unattended run must ship the marker, written by a person
# or by CI.
#
# The records nobody but their writer touches (design.md appendix). Paths are classified
# lower-cased: the default macOS volume is case-insensitive, so `.Praxis/Approved/c` IS the
# marker. Who is writing comes from the host payload: `agent_id` is present on every hook
# that fires inside a subagent and absent on the main thread; `agent_type` names the role.
#
#   .praxis/approved/<c>, .praxis/needs-human/<c>, .praxis/intent/*   never Edit/Write
#   specs/<c>/decision.md          the approver subagent only; never the main thread; never a
#                                  verdict of APPROVE (human) — only scripts/approve.sh writes that
#   specs/<c>/review/round-N/<lens>.md   its lens only (refuter-<lens>, lens-ui for ui.md); the
#                                  main thread may WRITE one whole file with `verdict: SKIP`
#                                  for a lens that never returned, and may not Edit one
#   specs/<c>/review/round-N/lenses      the main thread only; pinned once the round has a
#                                  review; must name correctness, security and tests
#   specs/<c>/implementation.md    the main thread only; `round:` never goes down — rework.sh,
#                                  run by the person, is the only way down
#
# Three gates ride on tools that carry no file path. Each reads only files under the
# change's record, never `.praxis/active-change` alone (the model writes that file):
#
#   Agent        a dispatch of `builder` — and, while a round is open, of any write-capable
#                role (engineer, backend, design, platform)
#   SendMessage  a resume whose `to` is the `builder:` SOME ledger records; with a round open
#                and no `builder:` recorded, every message is denied until it is
#                → no ledger: deny ("open the change first") · round 0: allow · round N with a
#                  lens file missing: deny, naming the missing lenses (the barrier) · round N
#                  complete, all PASS: allow · round 1 complete with CHANGES or SKIP: allow (the
#                  one fix round) · round 2 complete and not all PASS: deny (the cap). The round
#                  is the larger of the ledger's `round:` and the highest `review/round-N/` that
#                  holds a review, so a field written back to 0 reopens nothing.
#   Bash         a ship: `gh pr create|merge`, `gh api …pulls…|…/merge…`, or `git push` whose
#                refspec SOURCE (or destination) is `praxis/<name>`, or whose source is HEAD /
#                absent while the branch checked out in the command's directory is one. The
#                NAME comes from the branch, and its own ledger and decision.md are read: no
#                ledger → deny ("no change record for praxis/<name>"); `decision.md` at APPROVE
#                (human): allow; APPROVE with every lens of the current round at PASS: allow;
#                anything else: deny with the reason. `--all` / `--mirror`: deny.
#                Also: `scripts/approve.sh <c>` and `scripts/rework.sh <c>` run only while the
#                one-shot token `.praxis/intent/<approve|rework>-<c>` exists — minted by
#                user-prompt-submit from the PERSON's `/praxis:approve <c>`, consumed by
#                post-tool-use. And any segment naming `.praxis/approved`, `.praxis/needs-human`
#                or `.praxis/intent` is denied unless it is a plain read (cat, ls, test, rg…).
#
# The Bash command is read as the shell would, not as a substring (praxis_shell_segments):
# segments on `&&` `||` `;` `|` `&` `(` `)` and newlines; argv per segment; quotes removed;
# redirections (`2>&1`, `>/dev/null`, `>file`) stripped; `VAR=x`, `env`, `sudo`, `command`,
# `time`, `nohup`, `nice`, `exec` skipped; `bash|sh|zsh -c "<string>"` and `eval` re-read;
# `git [-C dir] [-c k=v] [--git-dir …] push …` parsed; `cd <dir>` and `-C <dir>` move the
# directory the branch is read from. `echo "git push"` is one token of an echo.
#
# DOCUMENTED GAPS, stated rather than pretended away (the Bash-path class, design.md Out):
#   - git aliases (`git -c alias.p=push p`, `[alias]` in any config) are not expanded
#   - GIT_DIR / GIT_WORK_TREE in the environment are not read; `-C` and `cd` are
#   - `$(…)`, backticks and `$var` are not expanded: a directory or branch the shell would
#     compute is one git cannot be asked about, and the gate fails open there
#   - a script or shell function that wraps git (`./ship.sh`, `make release`) is opaque
#   - wrapper options beyond the common value-taking ones (`nice -n`, `sudo -u/-g/-C/-p/-r/-t/-U`,
#     `env -u/-C/-S`): an unknown option that takes a value makes its value the command word
#   - Bash writes to the ledger (`sed -i`, `cat > …`) are not read: `round:` tamper from Bash
#   - the floor is keyed on the change NAME: `.praxis/active-change` pointed at another,
#     already approved change satisfies the floor for a source edit (approval is per change)
#   - Codex puts no agent fields on PreToolUse, so there every write looks like the main
#     thread's: lenses and the approver cannot write their files, and the cycle on Codex ends
#     in the person's `/praxis:approve`
#
# A deny must be followable by the model that receives it. It cannot read the plugin
# directory (in `claude -p` that is a refusal; interactively, a permission prompt), so on the
# first floor deny the templates are copied into the project as `specs/_templates/` and every
# step refers to that local copy. The required sections are repeated in the message so a model
# that still cannot read produces the right shape.
#
# `<active>` is `.praxis/active-change` when present, else the most recently modified ledger.
# An edit under `<root>/.praxis/worktrees/<name>/` — the builder's linked worktree — is judged
# by that checkout (its own `.praxis/` and `specs/`, seeded by scripts/worktree.sh; the ledger
# from the main checkout), because the host's project dir stays on the main checkout.
#
# A second gate rides on the edit event: the tier-1 comment pass (specs/comment-discipline,
# ADR-001/ADR-002). Only lines this edit ADDS are inspected, and the false-positive gate
# outranks the detection gate (ADR-005).
#
# Escape hatches: PRAXIS_FLOOR=off allows everything — floor, records, gates and comment pass.
# PRAXIS_COMMENTS=off lifts the comment pass alone. Those are the only two overrides.
#
# Fail-open on anything unexpected (no payload, unreadable path, a host that speaks a
# different dialect): the floor is about ceremony, not safety, so a hook defect must cost
# a missing record, never a blocked editor. Each such fall-through leaves one stderr line.
#
# Hosts: Claude Code reads allow / deny / ask. Codex reads the same nested shape but its
# reference says `ask` is "parsed but not supported yet", so on Codex the approval stop is a
# `deny` pointing at `/praxis:approve`. Codex reports `apply_patch` (paths from its `*** …
# File:` headers), its shell as `Bash`, `spawn_agent` as `Agent`; it has no SendMessage.

set -uo pipefail

SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
. "${SCRIPT_DIR}/lib.sh"
PRAXIS_ROOT="$(praxis_root "$SCRIPT_DIR")"

allow() { [ -n "${1:-}" ] && printf 'praxis pre-tool-use: %s — allowing\n' "$1" >&2; exit 0; }

[ "${PRAXIS_FLOOR:-}" = off ] && exit 0

payload=""
IFS= read -r -d '' -t 1 payload
[ -n "$payload" ] || allow "no payload"

tool="$(praxis_json_string "$payload" tool_name)"
case "$tool" in Edit|Write|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit|apply_patch|Agent|SendMessage|Bash) ;; *) exit 0 ;; esac

cwd="$(praxis_json_string "$payload" cwd)"
[ -n "$cwd" ] || cwd="$PWD"
root="$(praxis_project_root "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$cwd}}")"
[ -n "$root" ] || allow "cannot resolve the project root"

mode="$(praxis_mode)"
host="$(praxis_host)"

# Who is writing. `agent_id` is on every hook that fires inside a subagent (Claude Code hooks
# reference, common input fields) and on none from the main thread; `agent_type` is the role.
agent_id="$(praxis_json_string "$payload" agent_id)"
role="$(praxis_lower "$(praxis_json_string "$payload" agent_type)")"; role="${role#praxis:}"
is_main=0; [ -z "$agent_id" ] && is_main=1

# The change and its files under the current root. Called again when an edit re-roots into
# the builder's worktree.
resolve_change() {
  change="$(praxis_active_change "$root")"
  name="${change:-<change>}"
  ledger="$(praxis_ledger_path "$root" "$change")"   # the main checkout's, from a linked worktree
  spec="$(praxis_spec_file "$root" "$change")"
}
resolve_change
target=""

# The blank forms, project-local, so the deny points at files the model may read. Copied
# once, only on a deny — an allowed edit never writes into the user's repository. The
# CLAUDE.md -> AGENTS.md symlink survives `cp -R` on both BSD and GNU; where it does not,
# a plain copy stands in.
ensure_templates() {
  [ -d "${root}/specs/_templates" ] && return 0
  local src="${PRAXIS_ROOT}/specs/_templates"
  [ -d "$src" ] || { printf 'praxis pre-tool-use: no templates at %s\n' "$src" >&2; return 0; }
  mkdir -p "${root}/specs" 2>/dev/null && cp -R "$src" "${root}/specs/_templates" 2>/dev/null \
    || { printf 'praxis pre-tool-use: could not copy templates into %s/specs\n' "$root" >&2; return 0; }
  if [ -e "${root}/specs/_templates/AGENTS.md" ] && [ ! -e "${root}/specs/_templates/CLAUDE.md" ]; then
    cp "${root}/specs/_templates/AGENTS.md" "${root}/specs/_templates/CLAUDE.md" 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
}

decide() {
  praxis_trace "PreToolUse" "$1 ${mode} ${target}"
  printf '{\n  "hookSpecificOutput": {\n    "hookEventName": "PreToolUse",\n    "permissionDecision": "%s",\n    "permissionDecisionReason": "%s"\n  }\n}\n' \
    "$1" "$(escape_for_json "$2")"
  exit 0
}
deny() { ensure_templates; decide deny "$1"; }

# Same trailer on every deny: what is free, and the only way out.
trailer="Writes under specs/, .praxis/, agents/ are always allowed. Override: PRAXIS_FLOOR=off (env, session-wide)."
override="Override: PRAXIS_FLOOR=off (env, session-wide)."

# The content this edit carries, as the file will read: Write's content, Edit/MultiEdit's
# new_string(s), NotebookEdit's new_source, the `+` lines of a Codex patch.
new_content() {
  case "$tool" in
    apply_patch) praxis_added_lines "$payload" apply_patch ;;
    *) praxis_json_strings "$payload" content; praxis_json_strings "$payload" new_string; praxis_json_strings "$payload" new_source ;;
  esac
}

# --- The cycle's limits: barrier, round cap, ship gate ---------------------------------------
#
# Every decision below is read from files the roles write (design.md appendix); the hook adds
# only the message. A deny names the file that would open the gate and who writes it.

# A builder dispatch or resume against the change's effective round.
#   builder_gate <change>
builder_gate() {
  local c="${1:-}" round lenses missing not_pass
  if [ -z "$c" ] || [ -z "$(praxis_ledger_path "$root" "$c")" ]; then
    decide deny "PRAXIS: open the change first — ${c:+specs/${c}/implementation.md does not exist}${c:-.praxis/active-change names no change}. A builder is dispatched only inside a change: Write specs/<change>/spec.md and specs/<change>/implementation.md, Write .praxis/active-change with the change name, and get the person's approval. ${override}"
  fi
  round="$(praxis_effective_round "$root" "$c")"
  [ "$round" -gt 0 ] || exit 0                       # no review yet: the first build runs free
  lenses="$(praxis_round_lenses "$root" "$c" "$round")"
  [ -n "$lenses" ] || decide deny "PRAXIS barrier: waiting for specs/${c}/review/round-${round}/lenses — round ${round} is open and no lens list exists. The orchestrator writes it (one lens name per line: correctness, security, tests, + ui when the diff touches UI paths) before dispatching the lenses; the builder resumes only when every named lens has written specs/${c}/review/round-${round}/<lens>.md. ${override}"
  missing="$(praxis_round_missing "$root" "$c" "$round" | tr '\n' ' ')"; missing="${missing% }"
  [ -z "$missing" ] || decide deny "PRAXIS barrier: waiting for ${missing} — round ${round} of specs/${c} is incomplete. Each lens writes specs/${c}/review/round-${round}/<lens>.md (verdict: PASS | CHANGES) in its own context; the builder resumes only when every name in review/round-${round}/lenses has its file. A lens that never returns gets 'verdict: SKIP' from the orchestrator; SKIP counts as not PASS — at round 1 the builder may still resume for the other lenses' CHANGES, at round 2 the change goes to the approver. ${override}"
  praxis_round_all_pass "$root" "$c" "$round" && exit 0
  [ "$round" -lt 2 ] && exit 0                       # the one fix round (CHANGES or SKIP alike)
  not_pass="$(praxis_round_not_pass "$root" "$c" "$round" | tr '\n' ' ')"; not_pass="${not_pass% }"
  decide deny "PRAXIS round cap: 2 rounds done → approver / ESCALATE. Round ${round} of specs/${c} is complete and not all PASS (${not_pass}). A third fix round never starts: dispatch the approver, which records ESCALATE in specs/${c}/decision.md; the person then decides with /praxis:approve ${c} or /praxis:rework ${c} \"<note>\". ${override}"
}

# A push of a change branch or a PR against that change's decision.
#   ship_gate <change>
ship_gate() {
  local c="$1" verdict round not_pass
  verdict="$(praxis_decision_verdict "$root" "$c")"
  [ -n "$verdict" ] || decide deny "PRAXIS ship gate: specs/${c}/decision.md does not exist — nothing ships without it. The approver writes it (verdict: APPROVE | ESCALATE, with every check it re-ran) once every lens is PASS; the person can override with /praxis:approve ${c}, which records APPROVE (human). ${override}"
  case "$verdict" in
    "APPROVE (human)") exit 0 ;;
    APPROVE)
      round="$(praxis_effective_round "$root" "$c")"
      [ "$round" -gt 0 ] || decide deny "PRAXIS ship gate: specs/${c}/decision.md records APPROVE but the round is 0 — no review round ran. APPROVE ships only with every lens of the current round at PASS; without a round the person decides with /praxis:approve ${c}. ${override}"
      praxis_round_all_pass "$root" "$c" "$round" && exit 0
      not_pass="$(praxis_round_not_pass "$root" "$c" "$round" | tr '\n' ' ')"; not_pass="${not_pass% }"
      decide deny "PRAXIS ship gate: lenses not all PASS in round ${round} of specs/${c}: ${not_pass:-no lens listed in review/round-${round}/lenses}. APPROVE ships only with every lens at PASS, each with its 'What I tried to break'; a CHANGES, SKIP or no-evidence PASS goes back to the builder (round < 2) or to the approver for ESCALATE. The person can override with /praxis:approve ${c}. ${override}"
      ;;
    *)
      decide deny "PRAXIS ship gate: specs/${c}/decision.md verdict ${verdict} — only APPROVE (with every lens PASS) or APPROVE (human) ships. ESCALATE means the person decides: /praxis:approve ${c} to ship, /praxis:rework ${c} \"<note>\" to send it back to the builder. ${override}"
      ;;
  esac
}

# --- Reading a Bash command -------------------------------------------------------------------

re_redir_self='^[0-9]*(>>|>|<)&[0-9-]+$'            # 2>&1, >&2, 1>&-: one token, no target
re_redir_op='^([0-9]*(>>|>|<|<>)|&>>|&>)$'           # the operator alone: the next token is its target
re_redir_tgt='^([0-9]*(>>|>|<|<>)|&>>|&>).+'         # the operator glued to its target

# argv without its redirections.
strip_redirects() {
  local -a out=()
  local i=0 n=${#argv[@]} t
  while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
    t="${argv[$i]}"
    if [[ $t =~ $re_redir_self ]]; then i=$((i + 1)); continue; fi
    if [[ $t =~ $re_redir_op ]]; then i=$((i + 2)); continue; fi
    if [[ $t =~ $re_redir_tgt ]]; then i=$((i + 1)); continue; fi
    out+=("$t"); i=$((i + 1))
  done
  argv=("${out[@]+"${out[@]}"}")
}

# The index of the command word: past `VAR=x` assignments and the wrappers that run a command
# unchanged (env, command, time, nohup, nice, sudo, exec, builtin) and their valueless options.
command_index() {
  local i=0 n=${#argv[@]}
  while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
    case "${argv[$i]}" in
      *=*) i=$((i + 1)) ;;
      env|command|time|nohup|nice|sudo|exec|builtin)
        w="${argv[$i]}"; i=$((i + 1))
        while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
          case "${argv[$i]}" in
            -*) case "${w}:${argv[$i]}" in
                  nice:-n|sudo:-u|sudo:-g|sudo:-C|sudo:-p|sudo:-r|sudo:-t|sudo:-U|env:-u|env:-C|env:-S) i=$((i + 2)) ;;
                  *) i=$((i + 1)) ;;
                esac ;;
            *) break ;;
          esac
        done ;;
      *) break ;;
    esac
  done
  printf '%s' "$i"
}

on_branch_of() { git -C "$1" rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD 2>/dev/null; }
resolve_dir() { case "$1" in "") printf '%s' "$2" ;; /*) printf '%s' "$1" ;; *) printf '%s/%s' "$2" "$1" ;; esac; }

# What a ship command names. Set by ship_command when it finds one:
#   ship_kind   push | pr
#   ship_name   the <name> of praxis/<name>; for a PR off a non-change branch, the active change
#   ship_all    1 for `git push --all` / `--mirror`
ship_kind=""; ship_name=""; ship_all=0

# A `gh` segment: pr create|merge, or api touching pulls / merge. argv from index $1, dir $2.
gh_ship() {
  local i="$1" dir="$2" n=${#argv[@]} sub t branch="" j hit
  while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
    case "${argv[$i]}" in -R|--repo|--hostname) i=$((i + 2)) ;; -*) i=$((i + 1)) ;; *) break ;; esac
  done
  sub="${argv[$i]:-}"; i=$((i + 1))
  case "$sub" in
    pr)  case "${argv[$i]:-}" in create|merge) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac ;;
    api) hit=0; j="$i"; while [ "$j" -lt "$n" ]; do case "${argv[$j]}" in *pulls*|*/merge*) hit=1 ;; esac; j=$((j + 1)); done
         [ "$hit" = 1 ] || return 1 ;;
    *)   return 1 ;;
  esac
  while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
    t="${argv[$i]}"
    case "$t" in
      --head|-H) branch="${argv[$((i + 1))]:-}"; break ;;
      --head=*)  branch="${t#--head=}"; break ;;
      head=*)    branch="${t#head=}"; break ;;
    esac
    i=$((i + 1))
  done
  [ -n "$branch" ] || branch="$(on_branch_of "$dir")"
  ship_kind=pr
  case "$branch" in praxis/*) ship_name="${branch#praxis/}" ;; *) ship_name="$change" ;; esac
  return 0
}

# A `git … push …` segment: argv from index $1 (the `git` token), dir $2.
git_ship() {
  local i="$1" gitdir="$2" n=${#argv[@]} pos=0 refs="" ref src dst branch
  i=$((i + 1))
  while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
    case "${argv[$i]}" in
      -C) gitdir="$(resolve_dir "${argv[$((i + 1))]:-}" "$gitdir")"; i=$((i + 2)) ;;
      -c|--git-dir|--work-tree|--namespace|--exec-path) i=$((i + 2)) ;;
      -*) i=$((i + 1)) ;;
      *)  break ;;
    esac
  done
  [ "${argv[$i]:-}" = push ] || return 1
  i=$((i + 1))
  while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
    case "${argv[$i]}" in
      --all|--mirror|--branches) ship_kind=push; ship_all=1; return 0 ;;
      -o|--push-option|--receive-pack|--exec|--repo) i=$((i + 2)); continue ;;
      -*) i=$((i + 1)); continue ;;
    esac
    pos=$((pos + 1))
    [ "$pos" -ge 2 ] && refs="${refs}${argv[$i]}"$'\n'
    i=$((i + 1))
  done
  if [ -z "$refs" ]; then
    branch="$(on_branch_of "$gitdir")"
    case "$branch" in praxis/*) ship_kind=push; ship_name="${branch#praxis/}"; return 0 ;; esac
    return 1
  fi
  while IFS= read -r ref; do
    [ -n "$ref" ] || continue
    ref="${ref#+}"
    src="${ref%%:*}"; dst=""
    case "$ref" in *:*) dst="${ref#*:}" ;; esac
    src="${src#refs/heads/}"; dst="${dst#refs/heads/}"
    case "$src" in
      praxis/*) ship_kind=push; ship_name="${src#praxis/}"; return 0 ;;
      HEAD|"")  branch="$(on_branch_of "$gitdir")"
                case "$branch" in praxis/*) ship_kind=push; ship_name="${branch#praxis/}"; return 0 ;; esac ;;
    esac
    case "$dst" in praxis/*) ship_kind=push; ship_name="${dst#praxis/}"; return 0 ;; esac
  done <<EOF
$refs
EOF
  return 1
}

# Whether a command ships a change. Segments as the shell reads them; `cd` moves the
# directory for the segments after it; `bash -c` / `eval` strings are read the same way.
#   ship_command <command> [<depth>] [<dir>]
ship_command() {
  local depth="${2:-0}" dir="${3:-$cwd}" seg i n j
  local -a argv
  [ "$depth" -le 3 ] || return 1
  while IFS= read -r seg; do
    [ -n "$seg" ] || continue
    IFS=$'\034' read -r -a argv <<< "$seg"
    strip_redirects
    i="$(command_index)"; n=${#argv[@]}
    [ "$i" -lt "$n" ] || continue
    case "${argv[$i]}" in
      cd) dir="$(resolve_dir "${argv[$((i + 1))]:-}" "$dir")" ;;
      bash|sh|zsh|*/bash|*/sh|*/zsh)
        j=$((i + 1))
        while [ "$j" -lt "$n" ]; do
          if [ "${argv[$j]}" = -c ]; then ship_command "${argv[$((j + 1))]:-}" $((depth + 1)) "$dir" && return 0; break; fi
          j=$((j + 1))
        done ;;
      eval) ship_command "$(printf '%s ' "${argv[@]:$((i + 1))}")" $((depth + 1)) "$dir" && return 0 ;;
      gh|*/gh)   gh_ship $((i + 1)) "$dir" && return 0 ;;
      git|*/git) git_ship "$i" "$dir" && return 0 ;;
    esac
  done <<EOF
$(praxis_shell_segments "$1")
EOF
  return 1
}

# `scripts/approve.sh <c>` and `scripts/rework.sh <c> …` run only on the person's one-shot
# token. Any spelling of the path; the change is the script's first argument.
intent_gate() {
  local seg kind c i n
  local -a argv
  while IFS= read -r seg; do
    [ -n "$seg" ] || continue
    IFS=$'\034' read -r -a argv <<< "$seg"
    i=0; n=${#argv[@]}
    while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
      case "$(praxis_lower "${argv[$i]}")" in
        approve.sh|*/approve.sh) kind=approve ;;
        rework.sh|*/rework.sh)   kind=rework ;;
        *) i=$((i + 1)); continue ;;
      esac
      c="${argv[$((i + 1))]:-}"
      if praxis_valid_change_name "$c" && [ -f "$(praxis_intent_token "$root" "$kind" "$c")" ]; then break; fi
      target="bash:${kind}.sh"
      decide deny "PRAXIS: scripts/${kind}.sh is typed by the person — /praxis:${kind} ${c:-<change>}. That command mints a one-shot token (.praxis/intent/${kind}-<change>) only the person's own prompt can create; without it the script does not run, and the model has no way to mint it. Stop and ask the person. ${override}"
    done
  done <<EOF
$(praxis_shell_segments "$1")
EOF
}

# The marker directories are not reached from Bash either, except to read them.
marker_bash_gate() {
  local seg i n hit t
  local -a argv
  while IFS= read -r seg; do
    [ -n "$seg" ] || continue
    IFS=$'\034' read -r -a argv <<< "$seg"
    hit=""; n=${#argv[@]}
    for t in "${argv[@]}"; do
      case "$(praxis_lower "$t")" in *.praxis/approved*|*.praxis/needs-human*|*.praxis/intent*) hit="$t" ;; esac
    done
    [ -n "$hit" ] || continue
    for t in "${argv[@]}"; do
      if [[ $t =~ $re_redir_self ]] || [[ $t =~ $re_redir_op ]] || [[ $t =~ $re_redir_tgt ]]; then hit="redirect"; break; fi
    done
    i="$(command_index)"
    if [ "$hit" != redirect ]; then
      case "${argv[$i]:-}" in cat|ls|eza|bat|test|\[|stat|rg|grep|find|fd|head|tail|wc|file|diff|readlink) continue ;; esac
    fi
    target="bash:markers"
    decide deny "PRAXIS: ${hit} is a record the model does not write, from Bash or any tool. .praxis/approved/<c> is the person's approval (the host's ask, or /praxis:approve <c>); .praxis/needs-human/<c> is post-tool-use's record of an ESCALATE; .praxis/intent/* is the person's one-shot command token. Reading them is fine (cat, ls, test). ${override}"
  done <<EOF
$(praxis_shell_segments "$1")
EOF
}

case "$tool" in
  Agent)
    kind="$(praxis_lower "$(praxis_json_string "$payload" subagent_type)")"; kind="${kind#praxis:}"
    case "$kind" in
      builder) ;;
      engineer|backend|design|platform)
        # While a round is open, any write-capable dispatch is a builder resume by another name.
        [ -n "$change" ] && [ -n "$ledger" ] || exit 0
        [ "$(praxis_effective_round "$root" "$change")" -gt 0 ] || exit 0
        [ "$(praxis_ledger_field "$root" "$change" stage)" != shipped ] || exit 0 ;;
      *) exit 0 ;;
    esac
    target="agent:${kind}"; builder_gate "$change"
    ;;
  SendMessage)
    to="$(praxis_json_string "$payload" to)"
    [ -n "$to" ] || exit 0
    owner="$(praxis_change_of_builder "$root" "$to")"
    if [ -n "$owner" ]; then target="message:${to}"; builder_gate "$owner"; fi
    # Nobody's ledger names this id. With a round open and no builder recorded, that is the gap.
    [ -n "$change" ] && [ -n "$ledger" ] || exit 0
    [ "$(praxis_effective_round "$root" "$change")" -gt 0 ] || exit 0
    [ "$(praxis_ledger_field "$root" "$change" stage)" != shipped ] || exit 0
    [ -z "$(praxis_ledger_field "$root" "$change" builder)" ] || exit 0
    target="message:${to}"
    decide deny "PRAXIS barrier: a review round of specs/${change} is open and its ledger records no builder — record 'builder: <id>' in specs/${change}/implementation.md first, so a resume can be told from any other message. Until then no SendMessage goes out. ${override}"
    ;;
  Bash)
    cmd="$(praxis_json_strings "$payload" command)"
    intent_gate "$cmd"
    marker_bash_gate "$cmd"
    ship_command "$cmd" 0 "$cwd" || exit 0
    [ "$ship_all" = 0 ] || { target="bash:ship"; decide deny "PRAXIS ship gate: git push --all / --mirror pushes every branch, change branches included, so no change's record can be checked. Push the branch explicitly: git push origin <branch>. ${override}"; }
    [ -n "$ship_name" ] || exit 0                     # a PR off a non-change branch with no change open
    target="bash:ship:${ship_name}"
    if ! praxis_valid_change_name "$ship_name" || [ -z "$(praxis_ledger_path "$root" "$ship_name")" ]; then
      decide deny "PRAXIS ship gate: no change record for praxis/${ship_name} — specs/${ship_name}/implementation.md does not exist. A praxis/<change> branch ships only through its change's cycle: the ledger, the lenses' reviews and the approver's decision.md all live under specs/${ship_name}/. ${override}"
    fi
    ship_gate "$ship_name"
    ;;
esac

paths="$(praxis_edit_paths "$payload")"
[ -n "$paths" ] || allow "no file path in tool input"

# The builder edits in a linked worktree under <root>/.praxis/worktrees/<name>/ while the
# host's project dir stays on the main checkout. An edit in there is judged by that checkout.
worktree="$(praxis_worktree_root "$root" "$(praxis_project_targets "$root" "$cwd" "$paths" | head -n 1)")"
if [ -n "$worktree" ] && [ -d "$worktree" ]; then
  root="$worktree"
  resolve_change
fi

# --- The records: who writes what ------------------------------------------------------------

decision_gate() {   # <rel>
  local rel="$1" body verdict
  target="$rel"
  [ "$is_main" = 0 ] || decide deny "PRAXIS decision: ${rel} is the approver's record. The approver subagent writes it after re-running the acceptance checks, or the person writes APPROVE (human) through /praxis:approve <change> (scripts/approve.sh). The main thread never writes it: dispatch the approver. ${override}"
  [ "$role" = approver ] || decide deny "PRAXIS decision: ${rel} is written only by the approver; this write comes from ${role:-an unnamed subagent}. Report your findings in your handback and let the orchestrator dispatch the approver. ${override}"
  body="$(new_content)"
  verdict="$(printf '%s\n' "$body" | praxis_frontmatter_read verdict)"
  if [ "$verdict" = "APPROVE (human)" ] || case "$body" in *"APPROVE (human)"*) true ;; *) false ;; esac; then
    decide deny "PRAXIS decision: 'APPROVE (human)' is the person's verdict, written only by scripts/approve.sh when they run /praxis:approve <change>. The approver records APPROVE or ESCALATE. ${override}"
  fi
}

lenses_gate() {   # <rel>
  local rel="$1" dir f body missing="" lens
  target="$rel"
  [ "$is_main" = 1 ] || decide deny "PRAXIS review: ${rel} is the orchestrator's lens list; a subagent (${role:-unnamed}) does not write it. ${override}"
  dir="${root}/${rel%/lenses}"
  for f in "$dir"/*.md; do
    [ -f "$f" ] && decide deny "PRAXIS review: ${rel} is pinned — the round already holds a review (${f##*/}). The list is written once, before the lenses are dispatched; dropping a lens is not how a round passes. A new round gets a new directory. ${override}"
  done
  body="$(new_content)"
  for lens in correctness security tests; do
    printf '%s\n' "$body" | awk -v N="$lens" '{ sub(/\r$/, ""); gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/, "") } $0 == N { f = 1 } END { exit !f }' || missing="${missing}${lens} "
  done
  [ -z "$missing" ] || decide deny "PRAXIS review: ${rel} must name every required lens — missing: ${missing% }. The list is correctness, security, tests (+ ui when the diff touches UI paths), one per line; Write the whole file. ${override}"
}

lens_file_gate() {   # <rel>
  local rel="$1" file lens verdict
  target="$rel"
  file="${rel##*/}"; lens="$(praxis_lower "${file%.md}")"
  if [ "$is_main" = 1 ]; then
    [ "$tool" = Write ] || decide deny "PRAXIS review: ${rel} is a lens's file. The main thread records a lens that never returned by Writing the whole file with 'verdict: SKIP' in its frontmatter; it does not Edit a lens's file. ${override}"
    verdict="$(new_content | praxis_frontmatter_read verdict)"
    [ "$verdict" = SKIP ] && return 0
    decide deny "PRAXIS review: ${rel} is a lens's file and the main thread is writing it. Each lens writes its own review in its own context. The orchestrator writes one only to record a lens that never returned, with 'verdict: SKIP' in its frontmatter and the reason — SKIP counts as not PASS. Dispatch the lens, or wait for it. ${override}"
  fi
  case "$role" in
    refuter-*) [ "${role#refuter-}" = "$lens" ] && return 0 ;;
    lens-ui)   [ "$lens" = ui ] && return 0 ;;
  esac
  decide deny "PRAXIS review: ${rel} is written only by its own lens (refuter-${lens}, or lens-ui for ui.md); this write comes from ${role:-an unnamed subagent}. A lens writes its file and nobody else's; a builder reports in its handback. ${override}"
}

ledger_gate() {   # <rel>
  local rel="$1" c new cur
  target="$rel"
  [ "$is_main" = 1 ] || decide deny "PRAXIS ledger: ${rel} is the orchestrator's; a subagent (${role:-unnamed}) does not write it. Report in your handback and the orchestrator records it. ${override}"
  c="${rel#*/}"; c="${c%%/*}"
  new="$(new_content | praxis_frontmatter_read round)"
  [ -n "$new" ] || return 0
  new="$(praxis_round_number "$new")"
  cur="$(praxis_effective_round "$root" "$c")"
  [ "$new" -ge "$cur" ] || decide deny "PRAXIS ledger: round: ${new} is lower than the current round ${cur} of specs/${c} (the ledger's field, or the highest review/round-N/ holding a review). The round goes down only through /praxis:rework ${c} \"<note>\" (scripts/rework.sh), run by the person. ${override}"
}

record_gate() {
  local rel lrel
  while IFS= read -r rel; do
    [ -n "$rel" ] || continue
    lrel="$(praxis_lower "$rel")"
    case "$lrel" in
      .praxis/approved/*)
        target="$rel"; decide deny "PRAXIS floor: ${rel} is the approval record. It is written by the person — by approving the first source edit when the floor asks, or by running /praxis:approve ${name} — never by the model. Do not create or edit it." ;;
      .praxis/needs-human/*)
        target="$rel"; decide deny "PRAXIS floor: ${rel} is the escalation record. It is written by post-tool-use when specs/${name}/decision.md records ESCALATE, and removed when the person runs /praxis:approve ${name} or /praxis:rework ${name} — never by the model. Do not create or edit it." ;;
      .praxis/intent/*)
        target="$rel"; decide deny "PRAXIS floor: ${rel} is the person's command token, minted by user-prompt-submit from their own /praxis:approve or /praxis:rework prompt and consumed when the script ran — never by the model. Do not create or edit it." ;;
      specs/_templates/*) ;;
      specs/*/decision.md)              decision_gate "$rel" ;;
      specs/*/review/round-*/lenses)    lenses_gate "$rel" ;;
      specs/*/review/round-*/*.md)      lens_file_gate "$rel" ;;
      specs/*/implementation.md)        ledger_gate "$rel" ;;
    esac
  done <<EOF
$(praxis_project_targets "$root" "$cwd" "$paths")
EOF
}
record_gate

# The first source-side target decides; an all-spec-side write is free.
target="$(praxis_source_target "$root" "$cwd" "$paths")"
[ -n "$target" ] || exit 0

# Tier-1 comment discipline. It runs before the mode case because it judges the CONTENT of
# this edit, which is true or false independently of what `specs/` holds — one call site
# instead of one at each of the floor's allow points. Everything it can fail to understand
# (a tool it does not read, a path it cannot classify, an unparseable body) returns silently
# and the floor decides on its own.
comment_gate() {
  [ "${PRAXIS_COMMENTS:-}" = off ] && return 0

  local group added found kind line label
  group="$(praxis_comment_group "$target")"
  [ "$group" = skip ] && return 0

  added="$(praxis_added_lines "$payload" "$tool")"
  [ -n "$added" ] || return 0
  case "$added" in *"@generated"*) return 0 ;; esac

  found="$(printf '%s\n' "$added" | praxis_scan_comments "$group")"
  [ -n "$found" ] || return 0
  kind="${found%%$'\t'*}"
  line="${found#*$'\t'}"

  # The craft's own wording, verbatim: a second vocabulary for the same four patterns
  # would be a second standard. crafts/comment-discipline/comment-discipline.md.
  case "$kind" in
    code)   label="Commented-out code — git holds the history." ;;
    banner) label="Banner and divider comments — \`// =====\`, \`/* ---- */\`." ;;
    cot)    label="Chain-of-thought leakage — \`// Step 1:\`, \`// Now let's\`, \`// As requested\`, and anything else referring to the conversation instead of to the code." ;;
    todo)   label="A \`TODO\` with no owner and no tracker. What earns one carries either: \`// TODO(username): Describe what needs to be done.\` (Google C++) or \`# TODO: crbug.com/192795 - Investigate cpufreq optimizations.\` (Google Python)." ;;
    *)      return 0 ;;
  esac

  decide deny "PRAXIS comment discipline: this edit adds a line to ${target} that carries a tier-1 pattern.

    ${line}

${label}
The fix in every case is to delete the line. Re-send the edit without it; every other line in this edit is fine.
Only lines this edit adds are read — a comment already in the file is never the reason.
Override: PRAXIS_COMMENTS=off lifts this check alone; PRAXIS_FLOOR=off lifts the whole floor (env, session-wide)."
}
comment_gate

# The spec's shape, repeated in the deny for a model that cannot read the template. The
# template itself ships with factory-cycle (T05); until the plugin carries spec.md the deny
# points at design.md as the form to read, and still names spec.md as the file to write.
sections="Goal, Scope (In / Out), Acceptance (runnable checks: command → expected output; the approver executes these), Approach (files and the seam, no code), Open questions ([NEEDS CLARIFICATION] items; ready: true when none remain)"
spec_template="specs/_templates/spec.md"
[ -f "${PRAXIS_ROOT}/specs/_templates/spec.md" ] || [ -f "${root}/specs/_templates/spec.md" ] || spec_template="specs/_templates/design.md"

case "$mode" in
  fast)
    [ -n "$change" ] && [ -f "$ledger" ] && exit 0
    deny "PRAXIS floor (fast): ${target} is a source edit and specs/${name}/implementation.md does not exist.
1. Read specs/_templates/implementation.md, then Write specs/${name}/implementation.md in that shape (kebab-case change name): Status, one task line for this edit, Completed + verify evidence after the verify command runs.
2. Write .praxis/active-change containing the single line: ${name}
${trailer}"
    ;;
  *)
    if [ -n "$change" ] && [ -n "$spec" ] && [ -f "$ledger" ]; then
      praxis_approved "$root" "$change" && exit 0
      reason="${spec} is written and awaits the person's approval. Approving this edit approves the spec: the approval writes .praxis/approved/${change} and the floor will not ask again. On a host without a prompt, or in an unattended run, the person runs /praxis:approve ${change}. After approval, set 'stage: planned' in specs/${change}/implementation.md as the record — the stage unlocks nothing; only the approval does."
      case "$host" in
        claude) decide ask "$reason" ;;
        *) decide deny "${reason} (This host cannot ask, so the floor denies: stop and wait for the person to run /praxis:approve ${change}.)" ;;
      esac
    fi
    if [ -n "$spec" ] && [ ! -f "$ledger" ]; then
      deny "PRAXIS floor (${mode}): ${target} is a source edit and specs/${change}/implementation.md does not exist (${spec} does).
1. Read specs/_templates/implementation.md, then Write specs/${change}/implementation.md with 'stage: designed' in its frontmatter and the task list.
2. STOP: the first source edit after that asks the person to approve the spec.
${trailer}"
    elif [ -z "$change" ] || [ ! -f "$ledger" ]; then
      deny "PRAXIS floor (${mode}): ${target} is a source edit and specs/${name}/ has no spec yet.
1. Read ${spec_template}, then Write specs/${name}/spec.md (kebab-case change name) with: ${sections}. A legacy specs/${name}/design.md is accepted in its place.
2. Read specs/_templates/implementation.md, then Write specs/${name}/implementation.md with 'stage: designed' in its frontmatter and the task list.
3. Write .praxis/active-change containing the single line: ${name}
4. STOP: the first source edit after that asks the person to approve the spec.
${trailer}"
    else
      deny "PRAXIS floor (${mode}): ${target} is a source edit and specs/${change}/spec.md does not exist (nor the legacy design.md).
1. Read ${spec_template}, then Write specs/${change}/spec.md with: ${sections}.
2. Set 'stage: designed' in the frontmatter of specs/${change}/implementation.md.
3. STOP: the first source edit after that asks the person to approve the spec.
${trailer}"
    fi
    ;;
esac
exit 0
